**TL;DR** - _and overly simplified_ - Suspicious ticks represent off-exchange executions.

@Doggie52 -- @jaredbroad can correct me if I'm wrong, but if I recall correctly, this is a value provided by the data providers. I've always viewed these ticks as trades that aren't actionable for potentially a few reasons. _I think_ the most common reason for a tick to be marked suspicious is because it was reported from a non-standard liquidity pool. This could be an OTC trade reported up to 10 seconds late per [FINRA Rule 6282](http://finra.complinet.com/en/display/display.html?rbid=2403&element_id=4356) or even an execution that filled using [dark pool liquidity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_pool).

Due to the potential reporting time delay as well as the execution potentially taking place using dark pool liquidity, the data contained in suspicious ticks are often outliers and cause issues for fill models, consolidators, indicators and pricing of portfolio holdings.
